IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `emasa-authority`

-- Energy Market Authority of Singapore Act 2001, ss 5, 11, 12, 19A, 19B, 20, 27-30, 31 and First and Second Schedules -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_energy-market-authority-of-singapore-act-2001.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`wd a new solar import project` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `building a low-carbon energy project`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS FALSE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS FALSE

`wd reclaiming land` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `land reclamation for the Government`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS FALSE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS FALSE

`wd buying generation fuel` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `fuel for generating electricity`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS FALSE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS FALSE

`wd paying a project's recurrent costs` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `recurrent costs of a project`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS FALSE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS FALSE

`wd a write-off without approval` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `writing off a Fund investment`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS FALSE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS FALSE

`wd a write-off with approval` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `writing off a Fund investment`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS TRUE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS FALSE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS FALSE

`wd an old project already in service` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `building a low-carbon energy project`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS TRUE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS TRUE

`wd an old project not yet in service` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `building an energy supply security project`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS TRUE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS FALSE

`wd investing with stray project flags` MEANS Withdrawal WITH
    `purpose` IS `investing under section 15`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS FALSE
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS TRUE
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS TRUE

`ds a former employee leaking to a trader` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `by a present or former insider` IS TRUE
    `information obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `for the performance of duties` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`ds an officer answering a court order` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `by a present or former insider` IS TRUE
    `information obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `for the performance of duties` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS TRUE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`ds an officer briefing a licensee in the course of duty` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `by a present or former insider` IS TRUE
    `information obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `for the performance of duties` IS TRUE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

